Sval: Remove Firefox's New Tab add-on

Sval's own page serves about:home and about:newtab, so the New Tab
add-on and what served it only ran in the background: its
ActivityStream store, the about:home startup cache, the AboutNewTab
actors, the remote-renderer protocol, sponsored-link protection and
attribution, the contextual-services context id, the cached-OHTTP
protocol, the search hand-off bar it hosted, and the FirefoxHome
policy. The about: module, the new tab URL extensions override, and
the address bar's Top Sites, which the topsites module answers, stay.

